ants-terminal (0.7.80-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Post-0.7.79 follow-ups + small high-signal user-feedback
    fixes plus a build-OOM cure. Three notification/UI
    false-positives, a per-tab Claude: <state> widget bug, two
    refactors carried over from the 0.7.78 indie-review #2 sweep,
    and ANTS-1217 — src/*.cpp refactored into STATIC libraries plus
    build-time guardrails so cmake --build -j$(nproc) cannot OOM
    a 32 GiB host any more. Full ANTS_TESTS=ON build now peaks at
    526 MiB RSS (was >32 GiB OOM). 144/144 ctests green; 1/1 new
    claude_status_bar_per_tab feature test green.
  * ANTS-1161 — bottom-of-window Claude: <state> status-bar
    widget no longer shows another tab's state. Root cause: the
    singleton hook server's UDS is shared across every Claude
    under any tab, and ClaudeIntegration::processHookEvent
    mutated state and emitted stateChanged for every inbound
    event regardless of session_id. Fix: gate every
    state-mutating branch on the event's session_id matching the
    basename of the focused tab's transcript path. New
    4-invariant feature test claude_status_bar_per_tab.
  * ANTS-1214 — idle "Command Complete" notification no longer
    fires on every long-running command. checkIdleNotification
    now gates on m_grid->lastExitCode() != 0 (OSC 133 D exit
    code); successful commands and shells without OSC 133
    integration stay silent. Non-zero exits raise a "Command
    Failed" dialog-warning notification with the exit code.
  * ANTS-1215 — Review Changes button no longer stays active
    after every push because of an untracked `.directory`
    (KDE Dolphin metadata). refreshReviewButton now skips `??`
    lines in the dirty count; untracked files don't appear in
    `git diff` anyway, so the button shouldn't enable for them.
    Common false positives now silenced: .directory, IDE caches,
    swap files.
  * ANTS-1216 — bottom-right Tasks chip no longer lingers at
    "0/N" when every task is done, and a `deleted` task no
    longer counts as unfinished. Header-stated contract was
    "pending + in_progress"; implementation drifted. Fix:
    count-only-pending-and-in-progress + also hide the chip when
    unfinished count is zero.
  * ANTS-1181 — the 947-line setupMenus() in mainwindow.cpp is
    now an orchestrator of seven per-menu helpers
    (setupFileMenu through setupHelpMenu); About-Ants /
    About-Qt dialog bodies carved to their own translation unit
    (src/aboutdialogs.{cpp,h}) as namespaced free functions.
  * ANTS-1186 — Qt6 idiom polish (4 of 5 sub-findings):
    std::as_const(m_engines) direct value-iteration where
    appropriate; currentMSecsSinceEpoch() in place of
    currentDateTime().toMSecsSinceEpoch(); dead QDir projectDir
    removed; QColor::fromRgb(0xe74856) in place of
    QColor("#e74856").
  * ANTS-1217 — build-OOM cure (Phase 0 + Phase 1). Pre-fix:
    tests/features/ had grown to 141 standalone add_executable
    blocks each with its own MOC + its own copy of src/*.cpp;
    src/mainwindow.cpp was compiled 42 times per build, and a
    default cmake --build -j$(nproc) peaked above RAM+swap on a
    32 GiB host — earlyoom reaped the linker mid-write.
    Phase 0: ANTS_TESTS default flipped to OFF, Qt aggregate-header
    PCH added on the main exe. Phase 1: src/*.cpp refactored into
    six mandatory + two conditional STATIC libraries so each
    src/*.cpp now compiles **once** for the whole build. Layered
    three belt-and-suspenders optimizations: ccache as compiler
    launcher, CMAKE_OPTIMIZE_DEPENDENCIES=ON, and a JOB_POOLS cap
    (compile_pool=nproc-2, link_pool=2) so a future regression
    cannot OOM the host even on a naked -j$(nproc). Plus
    -gsplit-dwarf on Debug builds. Verified on the 32 GiB host:
    full ANTS_TESTS=ON build now peaks at 526 MiB RSS in 1m36s
    wall (was >32 GiB OOM); 144/144 ctests green. Phases 2–7
    (test-bundle consolidation via GoogleTest + workstation
    preset + safe-build.sh) pending — see docs/specs/ANTS-1217.md.

