ants-terminal (0.7.77-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * ANTS-1158 — Claude Code task-list status-bar widget + dialog.
    When the focused tab's Claude Code session has an active plan,
    a new status-bar chip shows <unfinished>/<total>; click opens
    a non-modal dialog listing each task with status (☐ pending /
    ◐ in_progress / ✓ completed) and a header
    "<N> tasks — <Y> running, <Z> outstanding, <X> done".
    Hidden when no plan exists for the focused tab.
  * Replays from ~/.claude/projects/<encoded-cwd>/<session-uuid>.jsonl
    in two modes. Mode A (TodoWrite snapshot): walk backwards from
    EOF in 64 KiB blocks to find the most-recent TodoWrite —
    avoids scanning the whole file to grab a near-tail event.
    Mode B (incremental): forward walk over TaskCreate (paired
    with tool_result for the allocated ID, mirroring
    claudebgtasks.cpp:222–243) + TaskUpdate flips, 16 MiB tail cap.
  * Filters out events with isSidechain == true (subagent tool
