ants-terminal (0.7.65-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Bundle G Tier 1 fix-pass. Two CRITICAL fixes from the
    2026-05-01 multi-agent indie-review sweep.
  * ANTS-1118 — smooth-scroll snapshot race. wheelEvent now
    triggers snapshot capture + scrollback-insertion pause
    on user scroll INTENT (positive m_smoothScrollTarget
    from offset 0 with no existing snapshot) rather than on
    committed offset transition. Closes a 16-32 ms race
    where the first smoothScrollStep tick produced no
    offset change (intStep = int(0.9) = 0), letting
    onVtBatch mutate visible viewport rows before the
    snapshot was captured. Spec at docs/specs/ANTS-1118.md.
  * ANTS-1130 — VT alt-screen + scroll-region invariants.
    Three findings folded into one fix-pass: DECSET
    47/1047/1049 split (only 1049 carries DECSC semantics
    per xterm ctlseqs); resize() preserves DECSTBM by
    clamping existing scroll region to new row range
    instead of resetting to fullscreen (TUIs no longer
    lose their scroll region on every window resize); alt
    scroll-region clamped symmetrically (previously
    unclamped — latent UB on next scrollUp after exit-from-
    alt with a shrunk window).
  * Two more Tier 1 items (ANTS-1131 PTY child lifecycle +
    ANTS-1132 IPC socket trust gaps) defer to 0.7.66 to
    keep this release's blast radius small.

