ants-terminal (0.7.53-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Tier-1 remainders + VT/paste/plugin hardening from the 2026-04-27
    indie-review. Six security-class fixes.
  * HIGH — VT parser dispatched OSC's trailing ESC byte as a real
    ESC sequence. A crafted OSC ending in `ESC c` triggered RIS;
    `ESC D` triggered IND; etc. Fixed at the C0 pre-handler —
    string-state ESC no longer transitions to Escape. New
    *StringEsc peek-states consume the trailing byte. Locked by
    tests/features/vt_osc_esc_discard/.
  * HIGH — X10 mouse byte > 0xDF corrupted UTF-8 stream.
    Coordinates clamped to 223 in X10 mode.
  * HIGH — Lua plugin permission allow-list + intersect missing.
    Manifest entries filtered against knownPermissions(); prompt
    result intersected with requested set.
  * HIGH — Image-paste filename injection + path escape.
    m_imagePasteDir canonicalised + required under $HOME; UUID4
    suffix on filename.
  * HIGH — Paste preview split on LF only — bare \r spoofed multi-
    line as single line. Preview normalises \r\n + \r to \n; actual
    paste still writes bytes verbatim.
  * HIGH — Bracketed-paste 8-bit C1 form \x9B[200~ not stripped.
    Strips 7-bit, raw 8-bit, and UTF-8-encoded 8-bit forms.

