ants-terminal (0.7.52-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First Tier-1 sweep of the 2026-04-27 indie-review findings.
    Eight fixes covering CRITICAL data-loss / security regressions
    plus HIGH security-class hardening.
  * CRITICAL — SessionManager silent data loss. saveSession +
    saveTabOrder used QFile::rename, which on POSIX refuses to
    overwrite an existing destination. Every session save AFTER
    the first silently failed. Switched both to std::rename
    (POSIX rename(2) — atomic replace), mirroring the 0.7.12
    Config fix. Errno logged on failure.
  * CRITICAL — Update-confirmation dialog same Wayland modal-grab
    regression as 0.7.50 About fix. Was QMessageBox::exec; now a
    non-modal QDialog + plain QPushButton + clicked→close.
  * CRITICAL — SARIF / HTML export not atomic + 0644 perms. Now
    QSaveFile + commit() + setOwnerOnlyPerms (0600).
  * HIGH — new-tab / launch IPC commands now route command bytes
    through filterControlChars by default (parity with send-text).
    raw:true opt-out preserved.
  * HIGH — OSC 8 file:// and ftp:// schemes removed from the
    hyperlink allowlist (RCE-adjacent / plaintext-creds).
  * HIGH — SSH extraArgs uses QProcess::splitCommand for
    quote-aware tokenisation, plugging the
    -o "ProxyCommand=..." bypass.
  * HIGH — extractCwdFromTranscript caps readLine at 64 KiB.
  * HIGH — AI endpoint scheme allowlist (http/https only).
  * HIGH — openFileAtPath argv-injection guard for paths
    starting with -.
  * Resolved (user report): GitHub Public/Private repo-type chip
    not showing — confirmed visible 2026-04-28.

