ants-terminal (0.7.51-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Hot-reload doesn't loop any more. Same-day follow-up to 0.7.50 —
    three reported symptoms (status bar permanently sticking at
    "Config reloaded from disk", Help → Check for Updates appearing
    to do nothing, Settings → Preferences not opening) all traced
    to a single root cause: MainWindow::onConfigFileChanged
    re-entering itself in an infinite inotify loop. The 0.7.31
    attempt at fixing the same loop
    (m_configWatcher->blockSignals(true/false) bracketing) never
    worked because Qt reads inotify events from the event loop
    *after* the slot returns — outliving the blockSignals window.
  * Fixed: Config::setTheme unconditionally called save() even when
    the value matched, so any applyTheme(m_config.theme()) from
    inside onConfigFileChanged rewrote the watched file → inotify
    event → next event-loop tick re-emits fileChanged → slot
    re-enters → loop. setTheme now early-returns when the value
    matches, breaking the loop at its source. onConfigFileChanged
    additionally skips no-op applyTheme calls and carries an
    m_inConfigReload re-entrancy flag (cleared via
    QTimer::singleShot(0, ...) so a save inside the slot is
    dropped but a subsequent genuine external edit is honored).
    The failed 0.7.31 blockSignals calls are removed.
  * User-visible: status bar stops sticking, Help → Check for
    Updates produces a visible toast, Settings → Preferences opens.
  * Locked down by tests/features/config_reload_loop_safety/ —
    INV-1 idempotent setter (call shape + functional mtime),
    INV-2 no-op skip at the call site, INV-3 re-entrancy guard,
    INV-4 failed blockSignals attempt removed.

 -- Anthony Schemel <aant.schemel@gmail.com>  Tue, 28 Apr 2026 10:14:52 +0200

ants-terminal (0.7.50-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Round four on the same dialog-button bug — and the matching
    Roadmap-dialog Close button. Three prior fix attempts (0.7.22,
    0.7.35, 0.7.49) each diagnosed a downstream symptom rather than
    the root cause; this release identifies it from upstream Qt
    bug reports and applies the fix that the bg-tasks dialog has
    been quietly using all along.
  * Fixed: both Help → About OK buttons (still) didn't dismiss the
    dialog in 0.7.49, and the Roadmap dialog's Close button hadn't
    worked since 0.7.43 either. Real root cause per upstream Qt
    bugs QTBUG-79126 ("Dialogs behavior on Wayland is wrong") and
    QTBUG-90005 ("global modality on Wayland"): Wayland's xdg-shell
    has no equivalent of Qt::ApplicationModal. Calling
    setModal(true) — added in 0.7.49 on the wrong theory — is a
    no-op on Wayland except for an aggravating side effect: KWin
    routes click events into the modal-grab handler which drops
    them. The role-based dispatch path inside QDialogButtonBox is
    a known second aggravator on the same bug. Both About dialogs
    and the Roadmap dialog now mirror the bg-tasks shape: non-modal
    QDialog + plain QPushButton + clicked() → close(). No more
    setModal(true), no more QDialogButtonBox in these three
    handlers. OK / Close clicks reach their slots and dismiss the
    dialog on the first try.

 -- Anthony Schemel <aant.schemel@gmail.com>  Tue, 28 Apr 2026 09:00:00 +0200

ants-terminal (0.7.49-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Three follow-up fixes to user reports against 0.7.48 — the
    About menu's OK buttons silently no-op'd again, the GitHub
    Public/Private badge wanted to live next to the git branch on
    the left, and the Background Tasks chip showed phantom counts
    of tasks that had long since exited.
  * Fixed: both Help → About dialogs now dismiss on the OK button.
    The 0.7.35 attempt only swapped the dialog type (QMessageBox →
    QDialog); both still went through exec(). On KDE/KWin +
    Qt 6.11 with the frameless + WA_TranslucentBackground
    MainWindow, the nested QEventLoop exec() opens does not
    surface the dialog as the active input window — the OK button
    never receives focus and the click silently no-ops. Both
    handlers now use the heap + WA_DeleteOnClose + show() +
    raise() + activateWindow() pattern that already works for
    other dialogs in this stack. About Qt dropped
    QMessageBox::aboutQt for a custom QDialog with the same
    treatment.
  * Fixed: Background Tasks chip now reflects only tasks that are
    genuinely running. parseTranscript performs a liveness sweep
    at the end — unfinished tasks whose output file is gone or
    whose mtime is older than 60 s are flipped to finished. The
    2 s status timer drives refreshBgTasksButton so the sweep
    keeps firing while the transcript itself is silent.
  * Changed: GitHub Public/Private badge moved to the left side
    of the status bar, next to the git-branch chip (was on the
    right via addPermanentWidget, shipped 0.7.45). Restyled to
    match the branch chip's rounded bgSecondary fill + border
