  * Lifecycle / cleanup. Three ROADMAP items addressing GUI-
    thread blocking on shutdown, an xdg-desktop-portal session
    leak, and two latent issues (OOM surface + symlink escape)
    in the Lua plugin loader.
  * Changed: PTY destructor escalation runs off the main thread.
    Pre-fix SIGTERM-then-busy-wait-then-SIGKILL ran on the GUI
    thread; N split panes closing together blocked window close
    N × 500 ms. Now: escalation moves to a detached std::thread
    capturing the pid by value. Cheap pre-escalation reap
    (SIGHUP + close master fd + WNOHANG) stays inline so
    well-behaved children don't pay a thread spawn. Synchronous
    fallback retained for thread-creation failure under
    ulimit -u pressure. Locked by
    tests/features/pty_dtor_off_main_thread (11 invariants).
  * Changed: GlobalShortcutsPortal closes its session on
    destruction. Pre-fix the class had no destructor — session
    handle leaked for the lifetime of the D-Bus client.
    xdg-desktop-portal accumulated one orphan session per Ants
    invocation that crashed or was SIGKILLed. Now: destructor
    issues an asynchronous org.freedesktop.portal.Session.Close
    call against the session handle when non-empty. Locked by
    tests/features/portal_session_close (8 invariants).
  * Changed: Plugin manifest cap + canonical plugin path. Was:
    unbounded f.readAll() on manifest.json (multi-GB manifest
    would OOM before JSON parsing); plugin scan used QDir::Dirs
    without NoSymLinks or canonical anchoring (tarball symlink
    could redirect init.lua loading outside the plugin tree).
    Now: 1 MiB manifest cap via bounded f.read; scan anchors on
    QFileInfo::canonicalFilePath, passes QDir::NoSymLinks, and
    per-entry verifies canonical containment inside the plugin
    root. Locked by tests/features/plugin_manifest_safety
    (12 invariants).

