    (isCatastrophicRegex, hardenUserRegex, applyFilter,
    loadAllowlist). Was: user patterns from audit_rules.json
    (dropIfMatches) and .audit_allowlist.json (lineRegex) flowed
    straight into QRegularExpression with no shape check and no
    match-time bound — a pathological pattern could pin the GUI
    thread for seconds with classic catastrophic backtracking.
    Now: nested-quantifier shapes rejected at compile time with a
    qWarning; surviving patterns wrapped in PCRE2's
    (*LIMIT_MATCH=100000) inline option for fail-safe step-budget
