    AuditDialog::isSuppressed, Finding::dedupKey). Was: SHA-256
    truncated to 16 hex chars (64 bits). Now: .left(24) (96 bits)
    raises the birthday threshold to ~2^48. New isSuppressed
    helper encapsulates a backward-compat lookup that matches
    either the full 24-char key OR the leading 16-char prefix, so
    existing pre-0.7.29 user ~/.audit_suppress entries continue to
    suppress new findings without forcing a migration. Locked by
    tests/features/audit_dedup_96bit (4 invariants).

